:- module(thmbr, [p/2]).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

% A GuardMatch at a rule head's rigid scrutinee pins T := list(B)
% with B itself RIGID: the matched value's element type is
% store-chosen, so nothing downstream may assume more about it than
% the match proved (spec §What evidence does). H is therefore typed
% at the skolem B, and `H + 1` — an overloaded operation — has no
% consistent signature there. The companion test
% typecheck_rigid_head_evidence shows what pinning it takes.
:- chr_constraint p(T, any).

p([H | _], R) <=> R is H + 1.
